-- title:
--   Base change of the coordinate presentation of Φ[p^N]
-- statement:
--   Let $p$ be a prime, $B_0$ a commutative ring and $\Phi$ a formal $\mathcal O_D$-module over $B_0$ in the sense of the project structure `FormalODModule`: a commutative two-dimensional formal group law $\Phi.F$ together with an action `Φ.act` of $\mathbb Z_{p^2} = W(\mathbb F_{p^2})$ by law endomorphisms and a law endomorphism `Φ.varpi` with $\varpi\circ\varpi=[p]$ and $\varpi\circ[a]=[\sigma(a)]\circ\varpi$. Fix $N\in\mathbb N$ and a commutative Hopf $B_0$-algebra $L$ presented by a surjective $B_0$-algebra map $\pi\colon B_0[\![X_0,X_1]\!]\to L$ whose kernel is the ideal generated by the two components of `Φ.act` $(p^N)$, such that each $\pi(X_i)$ is nilpotent, $\pi$ is $\bot$-adic evaluation at $(\pi(X_0),\pi(X_1))$, the comultiplication of $\pi(X_i)$ is $F_i$ evaluated at $(\pi X\otimes 1,1\otimes\pi X)$, the counit of $\pi(G)$ is the constant coefficient of $G$, and there are bialgebra endomorphisms $\rho_a$ ($a\in\mathbb Z_{p^2}$) and $\varpi$ of $L$ with $\rho_a(\pi G)=\pi(G\circ[a])$ and $\varpi(\pi G)=\pi(G\circ\Pi)$. Then there is a family $\theta$ assigning to every commutative $B_0$-algebra $S$ an $S$-algebra map $\theta_S\colon S[\![X_0,X_1]\!]\to S\otimes_{B_0}L$ such that, for each $S$: $\theta_S(X_i)=1\otimes\pi(X_i)$; $\theta_S$ is $\bot$-adic evaluation at $(1\otimes\pi(X_i))_i$; $\theta_S$ is surjective; its kernel is generated by the two components of the $p^N$-multiplication of the base change $\Phi_S$ along $B_0\to S$; the comultiplication of $\theta_S(X_i)$ is given by the $i$-th series of $\Phi_S.F$ evaluated at $(\theta_SX\otimes 1,1\otimes\theta_SX)$; the counit of $\theta_S(G)$ is the constant coefficient of $G$; $(\mathrm{id}_S\otimes\rho_a)\circ\theta_S=\theta_S(-\circ[a]_{\Phi_S})$ and $(\mathrm{id}_S\otimes\varpi)\circ\theta_S=\theta_S(-\circ\Pi_{\Phi_S})$; and the antipode of $S\otimes_{B_0}L$ composed with $\theta_S$ equals $\theta_S(-\circ[-1]_{\Phi_S})$. Moreover $\theta$ is natural: for every $B_0$-algebra map $f\colon S\to S'$ one has $(f\otimes\mathrm{id}_L)(\theta_S G)=\theta_{S'}(f_*G)$, where $f_*$ is coefficientwise application of $f$.
--
--   This is the functorial form of the coordinate presentation of the affine algebra of the $p^N$-torsion $\Phi[p^N]$ of a formal $\mathcal O_D$-module: the single presentation $\pi$ over $B_0$ is spread out, compatibly with base change, to all $B_0$-algebras, with the Hopf structure, the $\mathbb Z_{p^2}$-action and the uniformiser $\Pi$ transported along. It is the input used by [`CerednikDrinfeld.FormalODModule.exists_scheme_represents_subgroup_ideal_and_isClosedImmersion_toProjSpace`](thm.html#CerednikDrinfeld.FormalODModule.exists_scheme_represents_subgroup_ideal_and_isClosedImmersion_toProjSpace), where the functor of subgroups of $\Phi[p^N]$ is shown to be representable by a closed subscheme of projective space.
